    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1956736370178932976",
      "url": "https://x.com/Mirch_Tweets/status/1956736370178932976",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/Mirch_Tweets/status/1956736370178932976",
      "text": "Most infra talks about scaling like it’s stacking servers.\n@theblessnetwork scales like a swarm every new node adds muscle and mind.\n\nA browser node in Manila runs AI inference.\nAn old gaming rig in Berlin powers ZK proofs.\nA budget Android in Nairobi processes DEX orders.\n\nAll real time.WASM sandboxed. Fault tolerant.\n\nI’ve watched it self heal mid task four nodes drop in one country traffic reroutes instantly. No central controller.\n\nThis isn’t just efficiency it’s immunity.\n\nNo kill switch. No gatekeepers. No boardroom deciding who gets compute.\n\nAnd the best part?\nOnce you own your compute rail you can run anything AI agents games on chain apps no permission slip required.\n\nBless isn’t pitching the future.\nIt’s quietly building it behind the scenes right now.",
